# NestJS API (Contact & Extensions)

Optional **`backend/`** app — start with **contact form** only. Expand only when a measured need exists (newsletter, analytics).

## Scope

| Endpoint | Purpose | Priority |
|----------|---------|----------|
| `POST /contact` | Contact form → email to owner | First |
| `GET /health` | Health check for deploy | First |
| Future | Newsletter subscribe, view counter | Later — not without approval |

Do **not** build auth, CMS, or database layer for v1 unless explicitly requested.

## Module Structure

```
backend/src/
├── contact/
│   ├── contact.module.ts
│   ├── contact.controller.ts
│   ├── contact.service.ts
│   ├── dto/
│   │   └── create-contact.dto.ts
│   └── email.adapter.ts      # Resend or SMTP
├── health/
│   └── health.controller.ts
├── app.module.ts
└── main.ts
```

Flat, feature-based — no repository pattern for a single email send.

## Contact DTO

```ts
export class CreateContactDto {
  @IsString() @Length(2, 100) name: string;
  @IsEmail() email: string;
  @IsString() @Length(10, 2000) message: string;
  @IsOptional() @IsString() locale?: 'en' | 'fa';  // for email template language
  // Honeypot field — must be empty; reject if filled (bot trap)
  @IsOptional() @IsString() @MaxLength(0) website?: string;
}
```

## Controller vs Service

- Controller: validate DTO, apply throttler, CORS — no business logic
- Service: call `email.adapter`, map errors to safe HTTP responses

```ts
@Post()
@Throttle({ default: { limit: 5, ttl: 60000 } }) // 5 req/min per IP
create(@Body() dto: CreateContactDto) {
  return this.contactService.send(dto);
}
```

## Response Shape

```ts
// Success
{ data: { sent: true } }

// Error
{ statusCode: 429 | 400, message: string, error: string }
```

Never expose stack traces, SMTP errors, or internal config in production.

## Email Adapter

```ts
// email.adapter.ts — narrow interface
export interface EmailSender {
  sendContactEmail(payload: ContactEmailPayload): Promise<void>;
}
```

- Implement with **Resend** (preferred) or Nodemailer SMTP
- Env: `RESEND_API_KEY`, `CONTACT_TO_EMAIL`, `EMAIL_FROM`
- Email body: plain text + simple HTML; include sender email for reply-to
- Log success/failure at `info`/`error` — **never log full message content** in production if PII-sensitive

## Security

- `@nestjs/throttler` globally + stricter on `POST /contact`
- CORS: allow only `NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL` origin(s)
- `helmet` middleware
- Validate and sanitize all inputs; `ValidationPipe({ whitelist: true, forbidNonWhitelisted: true })`
- Honeypot field in form — server rejects non-empty
- Optional: Turnstile/reCAPTCHA later — not required day one

## Frontend Integration

- Frontend posts to `CONTACT_API_URL/contact` from Client Component form
- Show loading, success, and error states with i18n messages
- Fallback: `mailto:iamhosseinkhalili@gmail.com` link if API unavailable

## Health

```ts
@Get('health')
health() {
  return { status: 'ok', timestamp: new Date().toISOString() };
}
```

## Deployment

- Env validated at bootstrap with `@nestjs/config` + Joi/Zod schema
- Docker optional; can run as serverless function only if contact volume is low — prefer small Nest container on Railway/Fly/VPS

## Honest Full-Stack Story

This backend is intentionally **small and production-real** — suitable to mention as NestJS contact API work. Do not oversell as large-scale backend architecture.
